description.p:
Other objects, advantages, and salient features of the invention will become apparent from the following detailed description of preferred embodiments of the invention, taken in conjunction with the annexed drawings, in which:


Figure 1 is a generic information flow of a related prior art image editor;

Figure 2 is a block diagram showing general components that can be used with the invention;

Figure 3 is a graphic representation showing the variety of data types that make up an SI object;

Figure 4 is a graphic representation showing an example of the multiple representations (MR) that make up an SI object;

Figure 5 is a graphic representation of an image processing definition (IPD) as it relates to the output SI, which represents a structured description of references to component objects and image processing operations (IPOs) applied to those component objects;

Figure 6 depicts the flow of raster data during the rendering of an SI;

Figure 7 is a graphic representation showing how all child objects are merged into the parent pasteboard at the location specified by the MergePoint (relative to the object pasteboard) and the ControlPoint (relative to the child pasteboard);

Figure 8 is a graphic representation showing the pasteboard initializer function, in this case, initializing a pasteboard with a scanned text image;

Figure 9 is a graphic representation showing the communication path between the SI image editor and the SI structure editor;

Figure 10 is a block diagram depicting the SI display and re-edit functions;

Figure 11 is an example of a display screen depicting a current view of the SI image editor functions alongside an image to be edited; and

Figure 12 is an example of a display screen showing the associated SID file for the SI shown in Figure 11 graphically displayed in accordance with the invention.

IPOs are device independent descriptions of image processing commands. Certain fundamental functions (IPOs), described below, are preferred:


1) Transformer: spatially transforms the size or shape of an image (e.g.,affine, warp);

2) Formatter: converts pixels from one format to another (e.g., convert, interleave, cspace);

3) Filter: applies various filtering operations (e.g., convolve, median, morphological);

4) Colorizer: adjusts color value of images (e.g., relative, absolute, contrast, white-point);

5) Mask: apply mask operations (e.g., add, extract, convert, apply); and

6) Misc: apply other miscellaneous operations.

claim.claim-text:
A structured image (SI) editor for editing a structured image, the structured image being a raster image and including multiple data types, including individual SI objects, and a pasteboard that represents a frame onto which the multiple data types are rendered, wherein;
an individual SI object is a representation of data capable of being rendered into a raster image, each individual SI object having a tag defining its type and
the pasteboard has at least one component defining the frame into which each individual SI object is to be rendered relative to the pasteboard, said SI editor comprising: an SI structure editor operable to create a hierarchical representation of the structured image; and an SI image editor, coupleable to said SI structure editor, and being operable to display and manipulate said SI objects in real time, and to edit said individual SI objects while associating the individual SI objects with their respective high level representations.

Editeur d'image structurée (SI) permettant l'édition d'une image structurée, l'image structurée étant une image tramée et comportant de multiples types de données, y compris des objets SI individuels, et un panneau de collage qui représente un cadre sur lequel les multiples types de données sont restitués, dans lequel ;
un objet SI individuel est une représentation de données capable d'être restituée dans une image tramée, chaque objet SI individuel ayant une étiquette définissant son type, et
le panneau de collage comporte au moins un composant définissant le cadre sur lequel chaque objet SI individuel doit être restitué par rapport au panneau de collage, ledit éditeur SI comprenant : un éditeur de structure SI pouvant fonctionner pour créer une représentation hiérarchique de l'image structurée ; et un éditeur d'image SI, pouvant être couplé audit éditeur de structure SI, et pouvant être exploité pour afficher et manipuler lesdits objets SI en temps réel, et pour éditer lesdits objets SI individuels tout en associant les objets SI individuels avec leurs représentations respectives de haut niveau.
